## 5. `AuthStore` shrink

Drop `require`, `missing_required`, the `required: Vec<(String,String)>` field, and `ModelError::MissingCredential`. Keep `from_env`, `get`, `for_testing`, plus add one accessor the provider needs (`env_map`) so it can populate `HostRequest.env`.

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default)]
pub struct AuthStore {
    env: HashMap<String, Secret>,
    overrides: HashMap<(String, String), Secret>,
}

impl AuthStore {
    pub fn from_env() -> Self { /* unchanged, drop `required: Vec::new()` */ }
    pub fn for_testing(map: HashMap<(String, String), Secret>) -> Self { /* drop `required` */ }
    pub fn get(&self, provider: &str, key: &str) -> Option<&Secret> { /* unchanged */ }

    /// Plain `String` view of the env credentials, for forwarding to a host child process.
    pub fn env_map(&self) -> HashMap<String, String> {
        self.env.iter().map(|(k, v)| (k.clone(), v.expose().to_owned())).collect()
    }
}
```

**Call sites that still compile:** `derrick-assay/src/lib.rs:392`, `derrick-flow/src/code_review.rs:50`, `derrick-flow/src/steps.rs:296`, `derrick-adopt/src/lib.rs:181` all call only `AuthStore::from_env()` — unaffected. `derrick-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs:93-101` calls `require`/`missing_required` and **must be rewritten** (plan step 4 / step 6: replace the auth loop with the shared models-check core). `derrick-models/tests/models.rs` references `require`/`missing_required`/`MissingCredential` (lines 155-157, 206, 618-620) and must be updated/deleted alongside.

`ModelError::is_retryable` drops its `MissingCredential` arm — the remaining non-retryable set becomes `UnknownModel | UnknownRole | UnknownProvider | InvalidConfig`.

---

## 6. `resolve_role` / `ProviderRegistry::with_defaults`

The five host constructors are all `XHost::new() -> XHost` (unit structs). Register one closure per host name; each closure captures the host name and builds its adapter as an `Arc`. `shell` stays as-is.

```rust
impl ProviderRegistry {
    pub fn with_defaults() -> Self {
        let mut registry = Self::default();
        registry.register("shell", providers::shell::build);
        register_host(&mut registry, "claude",   || Arc::new(ClaudeHost::new()));
        register_host(&mut registry, "codex",    || Arc::new(CodexHost::new()));
        register_host(&mut registry, "copilot",  || Arc::new(CopilotHost::new()));
        register_host(&mut registry, "opencode", || Arc::new(OpencodeHost::new()));
        register_host(&mut registry, "aider",    || Arc::new(AiderHost::new()));
        registry
    }
}

/// Registers a host-delegated constructor under `host`. `make_adapter` builds a
/// fresh adapter each time a model is constructed (hosts are zero-cost units).
fn register_host(
    registry: &mut ProviderRegistry,
    host: &'static str,
    make_adapter: fn() -> Arc<dyn HostAdapter>,
) {
    registry.register(host, move |model_def: &ModelDef, auth: &AuthStore| {
        providers::host_delegated::build_for_host(host, make_adapter(), model_def, auth)
    });
}
```

This satisfies the existing `register<F>` bound: `F: Fn(&ModelDef, &AuthStore) -> Result<Box<dyn Model>, ModelError> + Send + Sync + 'static`. The closure captures `host: &'static str` (Copy, Send+Sync) and `make_adapter: fn()` (a function pointer, Send+Sync) — both satisfy the bound. `ProviderConstructor` (the stored `Arc<dyn Fn...>`) is unchanged.

`resolve_role` is **unchanged** — it already calls `ProviderRegistry::with_defaults().build(model_def, auth)`. The only behavioural change is which provider names resolve.

**`provider()` value must equal the host name.** Config's `ModelDef.provider()` now returns `"claude"`/`"codex"`/`"copilot"`/`"opencode"`/`"aider"` (per the `Config::defaults()` rewrite in plan step 3), and the registry keys match. The provider's `provider()`/`name()` accessors and the registry key are the same string, which is also the catalogue key and `HostAdapter::name()` — one identity across all four uses.

---

## 7. Error mapping: `HostError → ModelError`

```rust
fn map_host_error(host: &str, err: HostError) -> ModelError {
    match err {
        HostError::Timeout { seconds, .. } => ModelError::Timeout {
            provider: host.to_owned(),
            seconds,
        },
        HostError::NotFound { host: h } => ModelError::Provider {
            provider: host.to_owned(),
            message: format!("host binary not found on PATH: {h}"),
            retryable: false,
        },
        HostError::NonZeroExit { exit_code, stderr, .. } => ModelError::Provider {
            provider: host.to_owned(),
            message: format!("host exited with code {exit_code}: {stderr}"),
            retryable: false,
        },
        HostError::Io { source, .. } => ModelError::Provider {
            provider: host.to_owned(),
            message: format!("io error invoking host: {source}"),
            retryable: true,   // transient I/O — matches old subprocess.rs retryable stdin/stdout arms
        },
    }
}
```

Rationale: `Timeout` → `ModelError::Timeout` (preserves the `is_retryable() == true` behaviour). `NotFound` is non-retryable (a missing binary will not appear on retry). `NonZeroExit` is non-retryable, matching the old `subprocess.rs` which set `retryable: false` on process exit. `Io` is retryable, matching the old stdin/stdout write/read arms. `HostError` is `#[non_exhaustive]` — the `match` is exhaustive over current variants but if a variant is added later the match must gain an arm; consider a trailing `_ => Provider{ retryable:false }` only if you want forward-compat, but an explicit exhaustive match is preferable here so a new variant forces a deliberate mapping decision.

---

## 8. Trait-object / `Send + Sync` / lifetime pitfalls

1. **`Arc<dyn HostAdapter>` vs `Box`.** `HostAdapter: Send + Sync` (declared), and `run(&self, ...)` takes `&self`, so `Arc<dyn HostAdapter>` is `Send + Sync` and the `HostDelegatedModel` containing it is `Send + Sync` — required because `Model: Send + Sync` and the model lives behind `Box<dyn Model>`. A plain `Box<dyn HostAdapter>` would also work but `Arc` is the right call if the same adapter is ever shared; either compiles. **Do not** try to borrow an adapter out of a `HostRegistry` (`get() -> Option<&dyn HostAdapter>`) and store the reference — that introduces a lifetime tie to a registry the model does not own. Construct-and-own via `Arc` is the fix.

2. **`HostRequest` is `Clone` but holds `OutputSink` (an `Arc<dyn Fn ... Send + Sync>`).** The provider sets `output_sink: None`, so no issue. `HostRequest.env` is a plain `HashMap<String,String>` — cloning the captured `self.env` per call is fine.

3. **The two-event stream must be `Send`.** `CompletionStream = Pin<Box<dyn Stream<Item=...> + Send>>`. `futures::stream::iter(vec![...])` is `Send` when its items are `Send`; `CompletionEvent` and `ModelError` are both `Send`. ✅ No `!Send` capture sneaks in because we `await` the adapter before building the stream — the stream itself captures only owned `String`/integers.

4. **Awaiting inside `async fn stream` and the `async_trait` boxing.** `#[async_trait]` desugars `stream` to return `Pin<Box<dyn Future + Send>>`. Everything held across the `self.adapter.run(...).await` (`self: &HostDelegatedModel`, the `HostRequest`) is `Send + Sync`, so the generated future is `Send`. ✅

5. **`provider()` returning `&'static`-backed `&str`.** Covered in §3 — store `host: &'static str`, not `String`, to avoid any borrow subtlety and to share identity with the registry key.

6. **`Config::defaults()` is `PartialEq`-compared in tests.** Removing `endpoint`/`region`/`deployment`/`base_url` from `ModelDef` changes its shape; any test constructing `ModelDef { .. }` literally (e.g. in `derrick-config` and `derrick-models/tests/models.rs`) breaks. That is config-crate scope (out of my lane) but flag it: the struct-literal construction in `Config::defaults()` and tests must drop the removed fields in the same commit, and the `ModelDefLayer` loader must keep them `#[serde(default)]` + drop in `finalize` (plan step 5).

---

## Things in the plan that will not compile / need attention as written

- **`derrick-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs:93-101`** calls `auth.require()` / `auth.missing_required()`. The moment `AuthStore` is shrunk (step 4), this file fails to compile. The plan sequences the doctor rewrite into the same step — keep them atomic or the workspace breaks mid-step. The plan's "compiles at every step" guarantee requires the `AuthStore` shrink and the `doctor.rs` rewrite to land in one commit.
- **`derrick-models/tests/models.rs`** references `auth.require` (155), `auth.missing_required` (157), and `ModelError::MissingCredential` (206, 618-620). These must be deleted/rewritten in the same step as the `AuthStore` shrink, not deferred.
